PROBLEM STATEMENT:
Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return the k most frequent elements in the array.
The elements can be returned in any order.
AIM:
To write a Java program that finds the k most frequent elements using a HashMap and PriorityQueue.
JAVA CODE:
import java.util.*;
class Solution {
    public int[] topKFrequent(int[] nums, int k) {
        
        // Store frequency of each number
        HashMap<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();

        for (int num : nums) {
            map.put(num, map.getOrDefault(num, 0) + 1);
        }

        // Max Heap based on frequency
        PriorityQueue<Integer> pq = new PriorityQueue<>(
            (a, b) -> map.get(b) - map.get(a)
        );

        // Add unique elements to PriorityQueue
        for (int num : map.keySet()) {
            pq.add(num);
        }

        // Store k most frequent elements
        int[] result = new int[k];

        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            result[i] = pq.poll();
        }

        return result;
    }
}
INPUT:
nums = [1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3]
k = 2
OUTPUT:
[1, 2]
